{"type":"text","timestamp":1794276361118,"sessionID":"ses_e3cd18a48ffenKuVMJcQwTSrkz","part":{"id":"prt_1c333d272001XgvpNGFOneE54y","sessionID":"ses_e3cd18a48ffenKuVMJcQwTSrkz","messageID":"msg_1c333cc7e001nkIi9rmiDlrOqY","type":"text","text":"Great! All tests are now passing. Let me verify the implementation more carefully by examining what we've done:\n\n1. **Fixed `to_cents` function**: Changed from `int(float(amount) * 100)` to `round(float(amount) * 100)` to ensure proper rounding to the nearest cent.\n\n2. **Fixed `tax_cents` function**: Changed from integer division `//` to regular division `/` and added `round()` to ensure proper rounding to the nearest cent.\n\n3. **Fixed `Invoice` class**:\n   - `net_cents()`: Now applies discount to each line before summing\n   - `tax_cents()`: Now applies discount to each line before calculating tax\n   - `total()`: Now correctly calculates total by summing the net and tax cents\n\nLet me also verify that the rounding behavior matches the expected behavior in the examples provided in the problem:","time":{"start":1794276315762,"end":1794276361118}}}
