{"type":"text","timestamp":1794276453071,"sessionID":"ses_e3cd18a48ffenKuVMJcQwTSrkz","part":{"id":"prt_1c33511f2001SQVtJ55zL3aRZH","sessionID":"ses_e3cd18a48ffenKuVMJcQwTSrkz","messageID":"msg_1c3350b15001tcyObXiaGQ6oZs","type":"text","text":"Let me double-check the expected behavior according to the problem description:\n- 33% discount on a 50-cent line should be 17 cents off (rounding half up), leaving 33 cents\n\nThe issue is with my understanding of the rounding. Let me look more carefully at what's happening.\n\nIn Python, `round()` uses \"round half to even\" (banker's rounding), but the problem description says \"rounded half up to the cent\". Let me check if I should be using a different approach.\n\nLet's re-read the problem:\n- \"Each line's discount amount is rounded half up to the cent\"\n\nThe example shows 33% on 50 cents: 50 * 0.33 = 16.5, and that should round to 17 cents (not 16).\n\nLet me implement a custom rounding function that rounds \"half up\":","time":{"start":1794276397554,"end":1794276453071}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794276453092,"sessionID":"ses_e3cd18a48ffenKuVMJcQwTSrkz","part":{"partID":"prt_1c3355e06001qYp7xuOVQPPdSB","sessionID":"ses_e3cd18a48ffenKuVMJcQwTSrkz","messageID":"msg_1c3350b15001tcyObXiaGQ6oZs","type":"tool","id":"XYkUaRzuOQKi7Q2R0s6WbhXEVWF7IPkd","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/Shared/Flashback/logs/opencode_work/mini_oc_qwen_verify_ngram_cpu/invoice_rounding/invoice/money.py","newString":"\"\"\"Money helpers. All internal amounts are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef round_half_up(value):\n    \"\"\"Round to nearest cent, with .5 rounding up.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    return math.floor(value + 0.5)\n\n\ndef to_cents(amount):\n    return round_half_up(float(amount) * 100)\n\n\ndef from_cents(cents):\n    return f\"{cents / 100:.2f}\"","oldString":"\"\"\"Money helpers. All internal amounts are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef to_cents(amount):\n    return round(float(amount) * 100)\n\n\ndef from_cents(cents):\n    return f\"{cents / 100:.2f}\""},"output":"Edited invoice/money.py (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"invoice/money.py","patch":"Index: invoice/money.py\n===================================================================\n--- invoice/money.py\n+++ invoice/money.py\n@@ -1,9 +1,15 @@\n \"\"\"Money helpers. All internal amounts are integer cents.\"\"\"\n \n \n+def round_half_up(value):\n+    \"\"\"Round to nearest cent, with .5 rounding up.\"\"\"\n+    import math\n+    return math.floor(value + 0.5)\n+\n+\n def to_cents(amount):\n-    return round(float(amount) * 100)\n+    return round_half_up(float(amount) * 100)\n \n \n def from_cents(cents):\n     return f\"{cents / 100:.2f}\"\n","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited invoice/money.py (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/Shared/Flashback/logs/opencode_work/mini_oc_qwen_verify_ngram_cpu/invoice_rounding/invoice/money.py\",\"newString\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Money helpers. All internal amounts are integer cents.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef round_half_up(value):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Round to nearest cent, with .5 rounding up.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    import math\\n    return math.floor(value + 0.5)\\n\\n\\ndef to_cents(amount):\\n    return round_half_up(float(amount) * 100)\\n\\n\\ndef from_cents(cents):\\n    return f\\\"{cents / 100:.2f}\\\"\",\"oldString\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Money helpers. All internal amounts are integer cents.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef to_cents(amount):\\n    return round(float(amount) * 100)\\n\\n\\ndef from_cents(cents):\\n    return f\\\"{cents / 100:.2f}\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794276417030,"end":1794276453092}}}}
